From 9378691e53d6f0a1baca4e4befd83a4794de7d60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:09:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): age outbox stalls by observed awake operation
 identity [daveey]

Wall-created age counted laptop sleep as opportunity to send; last-round health survived that gap. Keep wall status truthful, but require the same sendable unanswered op for 600 monotonic seconds. Persist boot-scoped board observations, incident and warning state; reset on identity loss, unreadable data, reboot or observation gaps over 600 awake seconds. Preserve held FIFO/stale-wake and answered retry exclusions and replica-age handoff.

Proof: both entry paths failed before on 660 wall seconds with 60 awake seconds, now pass. Same-op awake stall, identity/ack/held/retry/read failure, boot and restart persistence, gap, memo validation, filing retry and delayed-read tests pass. Consumer suites passed (101 tests before final coverage additions); final suites and required CI recorded by ship. Fixtures do not establish deployed Mac behavior.
